     ppaasssswwoorrdd..lluuaa — bootloader password module

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     ppaasssswwoorrdd..lluuaa contains functionality for prompting for and checking pass‐
     words.

     Before using the functionality provided by ppaasssswwoorrdd..lluuaa, it must be in‐
     cluded with a statement such as the following:

           local password = require("password")

     The following functions are exported from ppaasssswwoorrdd..lluuaa:

           ppaasssswwoorrdd..rreeaadd(_p_r_o_m_p_t___l_e_n_g_t_h)    Read a password following a prompt.
                                           _p_r_o_m_p_t___l_e_n_g_t_h is required so that
                                           the twiddle may be properly drawn
                                           as the user is typing.

           ppaasssswwoorrdd..cchheecckk()                Drives the primary password checks
                                           done by the loader.  The
                                           ppaasssswwoorrdd..cchheecckk() function will
                                           check bootlock_password,
                                           geom_eli_passphrase_prompt, and
                                           password and prompt the user for
                                           passwords as-needed.  If password
                                           is set, the autoboot sequence will
                                           begin as the user is prompted for a
                                           password.

